// form-cli-local-plan.bml — a request becomes a band-first gap: a local voice writes it, Form verifies it before it
// is queued.
//
// A request (id, title, problem, needs, where, files, evidence: the shape learn/local-requests.jsonl holds) is handed
// to a local voice with the body's two honest bands and one queue row as its examples. The voice answers <plan> (a
// JSON object: id, band, full, writable, sources, definitions, checks), <goal>, <band> (the band file's text) and
// <reference> (the definitions as it expects the lane to write them). Form reads the plan and verifies it natively, cheapest first, before any queue row is written:
//   (6) shape: the plan reads; its id is a fresh kebab word; its band is a new file in form/form-stdlib/tests; full is
//       2^k - 1 and the band's head declares "Verdict <full>" (the band sweep's own reading); the goal names each
//       definition; a definition the file lacks carries its params; the band loads each writable file
//   (5) writable paths exist or are new under form/, observe/, gate/ or learn/, and none is a band; sources exist
//   (4) every check is a read-only tool call that fccw-rehearse finds meetable, and a check that pins text of a file
//       that exists (head, tail, read, cat) holds on today's file
//   (6) the queue row the plan makes reads back as native-turn-run reads it, and no queue row has its request, its
//       id or its band: a request is planned once
//   (1) before any run, a .fk band's parentheses balance (the line of a stray ')' or the count left open is the
//       failure), and it reads clean through the lane's arity tool (every Form word given the arguments fkwu's
//       reader demands), its lines returned as the failure when it does not
//   (2) the band, run on fkwu from a scratch tree over today's files, reads below full: the gap is open; it may read
//       nothing only while a definition it names is not yet in the file (an edit gap must read today's candidate);
//       a band that reads full is gap-closed, or moot when both of rung 3's stubs fail it (below)
//   (1)+(3) with each named definition a stub, once answering nothing and once its first argument, the band exits 0
//       within the deadline, prints a number, and that number is below full: it reads any candidate and fails a stub;
//       and no claim's bit stands in both stub readings, so every claim fails for a stub
//   (7) reachable: the <reference> block is required and holds each named definition, its delimiters balance (the
//       line of the reference where one does not is the failure), every check over a file that exists holds with
//       the reference standing (a check the change must break forbids the gap), and with its definitions standing
//       the band reads full, so the band, the goal and some candidate agree; the reference stays in the scratch
//       tree for guarded reuse; a compile failure quotes the line of the placed file the compiler names
//   (8) measured: with each named definition alone at today's text (the nothing-stub when it is new) and every
//       other standing as the reference, the band reads below full or a check over a file that exists fails (the
//       lane meets its checks as it meets its band), or that definition's change is unmeasured and could hide
//       behind its neighbours' stubs; full minus that reading is the definition's solofall, the claim bits it alone
//       owes, and the checks that fail its checkfall, both kept in the option's row and the queue row (a plan of one
//       definition reads its solofall from rungs 2 and 3)
// The scratch trees live under the caller's scratch directory: fkwu resolves a prelude in the "form/" root nearest
// the band before the checkout's own form/, so a stubbed copy of a writable file stands there and the checkout is
// never touched until the plan is verified. A refused option's tree is removed once its row lands; the verified
// option's stays for a review to read.
//
// A band that reads full on today's files is not always a closed gap that wasted the option. When the plan passed
// the shape, paths, checks and row rungs, the band reads its full today, a stub of each named definition reads
// below full (rung 3's two stubs, both) and the plan names the definition a moved request's fixborn stands in
// (findings-requests.bml: the change that moved the code the request cites, with the definition it landed in), the
// band measures that definition and today's files already meet it: the request is proposed moot. The option's
// scratch tree keeps the band, the walk ends there with status moot and the witness {kind, band, band_sha,
// band_text, defs, full, today, stubs, voice, option}, and the door writes that witness on the request's row
// (frq-record-moot). The row reads moot only while its fixborn stands, which the closing gate proved, and
// {"check":1} of the feeder door reads the row again: the band's text against its sha, the band on fkwu over
// today's files, the fixborn through the gate. A request with no fixborn, or whose fixborn stands in a definition
// the band does not name, ends gap-closed as every band that reads full does, and keeps its row. A stub that
// still reads full leaves the refusal gap-closed: the band measures nothing the definitions change.
//
// A plan that fails returns to the voice with the exact failure. The next option keeps the voice and lens (rung
// resume) and hears the failure and its own previous reply; the same failure twice in a row swerves: another
// lens (rung lens), then another local voice (rung voice). Each option lands one row in the caller's ledger with
// its approach {voice, lens, kind} and the digest of that approach (never of the feedback it heard, so a repeated
// approach repeats its digest) and the outcome digest, so fcgp-reading reads the walk as it reads the coding
// ladder: a declined walk asks the remote guide only when fcgp-earned? reads it earned, and otherwise ends with
// its why. A verified plan lands
// its band at its path and one row in the queue with origin "local-plan", the request id, and the planner's local
// generated and injected IDs over every option it took. A voice that answers "held" (the one GPU is another door's:
// flp-gpu-holders) ends the walk held, with no row for the option it could not take.
import form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-heal-native-report.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/host-walk.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/cell-said.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/form-agent-json-query.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/parse.bml;
import form-stdlib/meaning-codes.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-check-witness.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-guide-packet.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/findings-requests.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/native-source-inventory.bml;
import control/choice-lane-core.fk;
import form-stdlib/sha256.fk;
import form-stdlib/hex.fk;
section [form.bml] {
 class FormCliLocalPlan {
  // ── instruments ──
  def flp-attempts() = 6;
  def flp-deadline-ms() = 600000;
  def flp-roots() = ["form/", "observe/", "gate/", "learn/"];
  def flp-tests() = "form/form-stdlib/tests/";
  def flp-queue() = "learn/native-turn-queue.jsonl";
  def flp-requests() = "learn/local-requests.jsonl";
  def flp-dir() = ".hearth/local-plans";
  def flp-lenses() = ["band-first", "narrow", "edit"];
  def flp-prior-bytes() = 6000;
  // ctx: [voice, voices, attempts, queue, land, scratch, ledger, deadline]; voice(packet, name, option) answers
  // [status, text, prompt IDs, generated IDs]; land is the root a verified band is written under ("" = the checkout)
  def flp-ctx(voice, voices, attempts, queue, land, scratch, ledger, deadline) = [voice, voices, attempts, queue, land, scratch, ledger, deadline];
  def flp-ctx-voice(ctx) = ctx[0];
  def flp-ctx-voices(ctx) = ctx[1];
  def flp-ctx-attempts(ctx) = ctx[2];
  def flp-ctx-queue(ctx) = ctx[3];
  def flp-ctx-land(ctx) = ctx[4];
  def flp-ctx-scratch(ctx) = ctx[5];
  def flp-ctx-ledger(ctx) = ctx[6];
   def flp-ctx-deadline(ctx) = ctx[7];
   // Native care returns a released proposal or nothing. Verification and
   // publication stay in the planner; older eight-field contexts stay valid.
   def flp-with-reference-care(ctx, care) = append(ctx[:8], [care]);
   def flp-reference-care(req, ctx, said, refusal) = len(ctx) > 8 ? ctx[8](req, ctx, said, refusal) : nothing();
  // ── text ──
  def flp-starts?(s, p) = (len(s) >= len(p)) && ((String) substring(s, 0, len(p)) == p);
  def flp-ends?(s, p) = (len(s) >= len(p)) && ((String) substring(s, (len(s) - len(p)), len(s)) == p);
  def flp-head(s, n) = if (len(s) <= n) then s else substring(s, 0, n);
  def flp-join(xs, sep) = if nil?(xs) then "" else if nil?(xs[1:]) then xs[0] else mc-cat([xs[0], sep, flp-join(xs[1:], sep)]);
  def flp-lines(text) = split-on(text, "\n");
  def flp-sha(text) = hex-encode(sha256-stream-string(text));
  def flp-has?(xs, x) = any?(y => ((String) y == x), xs);
  def flp-first(xs, f) = if nil?(xs) then nothing() else if f(xs[0]) then xs[0] else flp-first(xs[1:], f);
  def flp-first-index(xs, f, i) = if nil?(xs) then -1 else if f(xs[0]) then i else flp-first-index(xs[1:], f, (i + 1));
  def flp-cut-at(s, mark) {
   let at = str_find(s, mark, 0);
   if (at < 0) then s else substring(s, 0, at);
  }
  def flp-last-find(s, mark, from, found) {
   let at = str_find(s, mark, from);
   if (at < 0) then found else flp-last-find(s, mark, (at + 1), at);
  }
  def flp-line-start(t, i) = if (i <= 0) then 0 else if ((Comparable) str_byte_at(t, (i - 1)) == 10) then i else flp-line-start(t, (i - 1));
  def flp-line-end(t, i) {
   let e = str_find(t, "\n", i);
   if (e < 0) then len(t) else e;
  }
  def flp-indent-end(t, i) = if ((i < len(t)) && (((Comparable) str_byte_at(t, i) == 32) || ((Comparable) str_byte_at(t, i) == 9))) then flp-indent-end(t, (i + 1)) else i;
  def flp-blank-byte?(b) = ((Comparable) b == 32) || (((Comparable) b == 9) || (((Comparable) b == 10) || ((Comparable) b == 13)));
  def flp-words-at(s, i, start, acc) = if (i >= len(s)) then reverse(if (i > start) then cons(substring(s, start, i), acc) else acc) else if flp-blank-byte?(str_byte_at(s, i)) then flp-words-at(s, (i + 1), (i + 1), if (i > start) then cons(substring(s, start, i), acc) else acc) else flp-words-at(s, (i + 1), start, acc);
  def flp-words(s) = flp-words-at(s, 0, 0, []);
  def flp-number-at(s, i) {
   let e = digits-end(s, i);
   if (e > i) then str_to_int(substring(s, i, e)) else nothing();
  }
  def flp-show(v) = if nothing?(v) then "nothing" else v.str();
  // ── JSON fields: a string, or the JSON of anything else; a field absent reads "" ──
  def flp-text(doc, key) = if (!fcgp-present?(doc, key)) then "" else if fcgp-str-node?(json-object-get(doc, key)) then json-string-value(json-object-get(doc, key)) else json-emit(json-object-get(doc, key));
  def flp-strings(n) = if fcgp-str-node?(n) then [json-string-value(n)] else if fcgp-array?(n) then map(e => if fcgp-str-node?(e) then json-string-value(e) else "", json-array-elements(n)) else [];
  def flp-strs(doc, key) = if fcgp-present?(doc, key) then flp-strings(json-object-get(doc, key)) else [];
  def flp-json-strings(xs) = json-node-array(map(x => json-node-string(x), xs));
  // ── the request ──
  def flp-clean-path(p) = trim(flp-cut-at(flp-cut-at(trim(p), ":"), " "));
  def flp-req-id(req) = flp-text(req, "id");
  def flp-req-files(req) = filter(p => (len(p) > 0), map(p => flp-clean-path(p), flp-strs(req, "files")));
  def flp-kebab-byte?(b) = ((b >= 97) && (b <= 122)) || (((b >= 48) && (b <= 57)) || ((Comparable) b == 45));
  def flp-kebab-at?(s, i) = if (i >= len(s)) then true else if flp-kebab-byte?(str_byte_at(s, i)) then flp-kebab-at?(s, (i + 1)) else false;
  def flp-kebab?(s) = if ((Comparable) len(s) == 0) then false else if (len(s) > 64) then false else if ((str_byte_at(s, 0) < 97) || (str_byte_at(s, 0) > 122)) then false else flp-kebab-at?(s, 0);
  def flp-safe-id(req) = if flp-kebab?(flp-req-id(req)) then flp-req-id(req) else "request";
  // a moved request (findings-requests.bml) carries the change that moved the code its where cites: the voice reads
  // it, and today's file, before it asks for a change that may already stand
  def flp-fixed-def(req) = if fcgp-present?(req, "fixborn") then fcgp-str(fcgp-obj(req, "fixborn"), "def") else "";
  def flp-fixed-key(req) = if ((Comparable) len(flp-fixed-def(req)) > 0) then mc-cat([fcgp-str(fcgp-obj(req, "fixborn"), "path"), ":", flp-fixed-def(req)]) else "";
  def flp-fix-text(req) = if fcgp-present?(req, "fixborn") then mc-cat(["since its review: commit ", fcgp-str(fcgp-obj(req, "fixborn"), "commit"), " changed ", fcgp-str(fcgp-obj(req, "fixborn"), "path"), " (lines ", fcgp-str(fcgp-obj(req, "fixborn"), "span"), " as the review read them) and wrote: ", fcgp-str(fcgp-obj(req, "fixborn"), "needle"), "\nThe request may already be healed: write the band that measures exactly what it needs", if ((Comparable) len(flp-fixed-def(req)) > 0) then mc-cat([", over ", flp-fixed-def(req), ", the definition that change stands in"]) else "", ". If today's files already meet it, your band reads its full today and Form takes the request as moot once the gate that proved that change agrees; a band over another definition leaves the request as it was. Describe the need as written and do not invent another.\n"]) else "";
  def flp-request-text(req) = mc-cat(["id: ", flp-text(req, "id"), "\ntitle: ", flp-text(req, "title"), "\nproblem: ", flp-text(req, "problem"), "\nneeds: ", flp-text(req, "needs"), "\nwhere: ", flp-text(req, "where"), "\nfiles: ", flp-join(flp-req-files(req), ", "), "\nevidence: ", flp-text(req, "evidence"), "\n", flp-fix-text(req)]);
  // ── the packet the voice reads ──
  def flp-exists?(path) = file_size(path) >= 0;
  def flp-is-dir?(path) = (Comparable) fs_is_dir(path) == 1;
  def flp-file-block(req, path) = if (!flp-exists?(path)) then mc-cat(["The file ", path, " does not exist yet.\n\n"]) else if flp-is-dir?(path) then mc-cat([path, " is a directory.\n\n"]) else flp-file-text(path, fhn-read(path), flp-where-lines(req, path));
  // The validator and its callers remain visible; a signature is not their contract.
  def flp-file-text(path, text, at) = mc-cat(["The file ", path, " reads in full:\n", text, "\n\n"]);
  // the line numbers the request's where names in path ("<path>:<n>" or "<basename>:<n>"), three at most
  def flp-where-line(entry, path) {
   let colon = str_find(entry, ":", 0);
   let named = if (colon <= 0) then "" else substring(entry, 0, colon);
   if ((Comparable) len(named) == 0) then nothing() else if (((String) named == path) || flp-ends?(path, ("/" ++ named))) then flp-number-at(entry, (colon + 1)) else nothing();
  }
  def flp-where-lines(req, path) = take(3, filter(n => (!nothing?(n)), map(e => flp-where-line(trim(e), path), flp-strs(req, "where"))));
  def flp-files-block(req) = mc-cat(map(p => flp-file-block(req, p), flp-req-files(req)));
  def flp-names(text) = flp-lines(text) |> map(trim) |> filter(line=>flp-starts?(line,"def ")) |> map(line=>trim(flp-cut-at(substring(line,4,len(line)),"(")));
  def flp-source-names(paths) = foldl((names,path)=>append(names,flp-names(fhn-read(path))),[],paths);
  def flp-focus-prompt(req) = "Select the existing entry functions whose behavior this task must change. Use only names in the catalog. Do not implement code or add helpers. Return only a JSON array of the selected function names.\nTask: " + flp-text(req,"needs") + "\nCatalog: " + flp-join(flp-source-names(flp-req-files(req)),", ");
  def flp-focus-path(req) = flp-dir() + "/focus/" + flp-sha(flp-focus-prompt(req)) + ".json";
  def flp-guided-focus(req) {
   let held=fhn-read(flp-focus-path(req));
   let row=faj-valid(held) ? parse-json("source-focus",held) : json-node-object([]);
   let text=flp-text(row,"text");
   let value=faj-valid(text) ? parse-json("source-focus-names",text) : json-node-null();
   let selected=fcgp-array?(value) ? flp-strings(value) : [];
   let names=flp-source-names(flp-req-files(req));
   flp-text(row,"prompt")==flp-focus-prompt(req) && flp-text(row,"status")=="answered" && fcgp-num(row,"complete")==1 && fcgp-num(row,"released")==1 && !nil?(selected) && len(selected)==len(json-array-elements(value)) && !any?(name=>!flp-has?(names,name),selected) ? selected : [];
  }
  def flp-focus(req) {
   let names=flp-source-names(flp-req-files(req));
   let named=names |> filter(name=>str_find(flp-text(req,"needs"),name,0)>=0);
   let guided=nil?(named) ? flp-guided-focus(req) : [];
   !nil?(named) ? named : !nil?(guided) ? guided : names;
  }
  def flp-caller-closure(defs,selected) {
   let body=mc-cat(selected |> map(d=>d[1]));
   let next=defs |> filter(d=>any?(held=>held[0]==d[0],selected) || str_find(body,d[0],0)>=0);
   len(next)==len(selected) ? selected : flp-caller-closure(defs,next);
  }
  def flp-caller-text(text,names) {
   let defs=flp-names(text) |> map(name=>[name,flp-ref-text(text,[name,[],""],true) ?? ""]);
   let roots=defs |> filter(d=>any?(name=>str_find(d[1],name,0)>=0,names));
   let section=str_find(text,"section [",0);
   (section<0 ? "" : substring(text,0,section)) + mc-cat(flp-caller-closure(defs,roots) |> map(d=>d[1] + "\n\n"));
  }
  def flp-callers(req) {
   let paths=flp-req-files(req); let names=flp-focus(req);
   let files=split-on(nsi-text(nsi-git()),byte_to_str(0)) |> filter(path=>flp-starts?(path,"form/form-stdlib/bml/") && flp-ends?(path,".bml") && !flp-has?(paths,path));
   files |> map(path=>[path,fhn-read(path)]) |> filter(source=>any?(name=>str_find(source[1],name + "(",0)>=0,names)) |> map(source=>[source[0],flp-caller-text(source[1],names)]);
  }
  def flp-callers-block(req) = mc-cat(flp-callers(req) |> map(source=>"Read-only caller definitions and their local dependency closure in " + source[0] + ":\n" + source[1] + "\n\n"));
  def flp-queue-lines(path) = if (file_size(path) < 1) then [] else filter(l => (len(trim(l)) > 0), flp-lines(fhn-read(path)));
  def flp-queue-rows(path) = map(l => if fcgp-object-line?(trim(l)) then parse-json("queue-row", trim(l)) else json-node-object([]), flp-queue-lines(path));
  def flp-intro() = "Implement the original task in native BML. Supply the whole changed definitions and behavior cases; Form owns compilation, verification and publication. A candidate must change the requested behavior, preserve its callers, and pass cases that fail on today's implementation and on stubs. Repeating unchanged code cannot implement a change.";
  def flp-lens-text(lens) = lens=="narrow" ? "Lens: narrow. Focus on the smallest change that serves the original task; preserve its complete contract." : lens=="edit" ? "Lens: an existing definition. Follow the existing entry and its callers. Keep observed contracts and repair the actual operation." : "Choose behavior cases first, then implement the behavior they require. Form builds the executable witness.";
  def flp-feedback-block(feedback, prior) = if ((Comparable) len(trim(feedback)) == 0) then "" else mc-cat(["\nYour previous plan was refused by Form's verification. The exact failure:\n", feedback, if ((Comparable) len(trim(prior)) == 0) then "" else mc-cat(["\n\nYour rejected candidate:\n", flp-head(prior, flp-prior-bytes())]), "\n\nRecheck the original request against the current source and callers. The rejected candidate is not a contract: preserve only observed successes, not unchecked assumptions. When improving an existing operation, change and verify its existing entry or caller; a new uncalled helper does not improve that operation. Derive required fields and defaults from the actual validator, and construct inputs in its actual native data type. Write the whole reply again with the failure removed and the original operation improved.\n"]);
  def flp-case-words() = "Form writes the executable witness from your cases; write no proof scaffolding. Each call is a pure BML expression exercising the changed operation. equals is its expected JSON scalar or nested array. Form prints the actual results and checks every case, the unchanged implementation, both stubs and each definition's contribution. All cases together read 1; a failed case reads 0. Do not change the original task to fit a candidate. Preserve callers, optional fields and existing specialized behavior. A new helper needs its existing caller changed and observed too. BML: def name(args) = expression; or def name(args) { let x=expression; final_expression; }. Every if has then and else. Lambdas use =>. Lists are [a,b], indexing xs[0], tail xs[1:]. filter, map and foldl return values; append never mutates a binding. There is no C-style for loop. JSON objects are native nodes constructed with parse-json or json-node-object, not ordinary lists. Read the actual source for available function names and signatures.";
  def flp-case-reply() = "Start with <plan>; emit only four completed blocks. <plan> is a JSON object with id,writable,sources,definitions with name and params; include every changed definition and new helper. <goal> states the original behavior. <cases> is a JSON array of {function,arguments,equals}: function is its existing name, arguments its values, equals the expected scalar or nested array. Form generates native calls: objects become JSON nodes, arrays become Form lists, null becomes nothing(). Use JSON null in this transport, never nothing(). Example: {\"function\":\"len\",\"arguments\":[[1,2]],\"equals\":2}. Complex compositions may use {call,equals} instead. <reference> contains complete changed BML definitions. Close every block. Form owns witness paths, executable text, full and source checks; supply none. sources names read-only dependencies. Measure changed operations through their callers; use real source/catalog paths for file cases. Preserve original behavior outside the task. No invented aliases, detached helpers or unchanged definitions in the manifest.";
  def flp-packet(req, lens, feedback, prior, queue) = mc-cat([flp-intro(), "\n\n", flp-case-words(), "\nThe witness imports form-stdlib/core.fk. Use start .. end for end-exclusive integer ranges, such as 0 .. len(xs); never enumerate a dynamic index range as literals. substring(text,start,end) also uses an exclusive end, not a length. str_byte_at(text,index) returns the integer byte.\n", flp-lens-text(lens), "\n\nThe request:\n", flp-request-text(req), "\n", flp-files-block(req), "\n", flp-callers-block(req), flp-case-reply(), flp-feedback-block(feedback, prior), "\nThe original task and current observations take precedence:\n", flp-text(req,"needs"), "\n", flp-text(req,"evidence")]);
  // ── the reply: <plan>, <goal> and <band> ──
  def flp-unfence(s) {
   let t = trim(s);
   let opened = if flp-starts?(t, "```") then trim(fcgp-after-line(t)) else t;
   if flp-ends?(opened, "```") then trim(substring(opened, 0, (len(opened) - 3))) else opened;
  }
  def flp-block(t, tag) {
   let open = mc-cat(["<", tag, ">"]);
   let close = mc-cat(["</", tag, ">"]);
   let a = str_find(t, open, 0);
   let b = if (a < 0) then -1 else str_find(t, close, (a + len(open)));
   if ((a < 0) || (b < 0)) then nothing() else flp-unfence(substring(t, (a + len(open)), b));
  }
  // a plan: [id, band, full, writable, sources, definitions, checks node, goal, band text, reference text]
  def flp-plan(id, band, full, writable, sources, defs, checks, goal, text, reference) = [id, band, full, writable, sources, defs, checks, goal, text, reference];
  def flp-p-id(p) = p[0];
  def flp-p-band(p) = p[1];
  def flp-p-full(p) = p[2];
  def flp-p-writable(p) = p[3];
  def flp-p-sources(p) = p[4];
  def flp-p-defs(p) = p[5];
  def flp-p-checks(p) = p[6];
  def flp-p-goal(p) = p[7];
  def flp-p-text(p) = p[8];
  def flp-p-reference(p) = p[9];
  // a definition: [name, params or nothing, file]
  def flp-default-file(writable) = if nil?(writable) then "" else writable[0];
  def flp-def-of(n, writable) = if fcgp-str-node?(n) then [json-string-value(n), nothing(), flp-default-file(writable)] else if (!fcgp-object?(n)) then ["", nothing(), ""] else [fcgp-str(n, "name"), if fcgp-present?(n, "params") then flp-strings(json-object-get(n, "params")) else nothing(), if ((Comparable) len(fcgp-str(n, "file")) > 0) then fcgp-str(n, "file") else flp-default-file(writable)];
  def flp-defs-of(obj, writable) = if (fcgp-present?(obj, "definitions") && fcgp-array?(json-object-get(obj, "definitions"))) then map(n => flp-def-of(n, writable), json-array-elements(json-object-get(obj, "definitions"))) else [];
  // [kind, text, plan]: kind "" when the reply reads as a plan
  def flp-parse(reply) {
   let head = flp-block(reply, "plan");
   let goal = flp-block(reply, "goal");
   let band = flp-block(reply, "band");
   let reference = flp-block(reply, "reference") ?? "";
   if nothing?(head) then ["plan-unreadable", "The reply has no <plan>...</plan> block.", []] else if (!faj-valid(head)) then ["plan-unreadable", mc-cat(["The <plan> block is not one valid JSON object: ", flp-head(head, 300)]), []] else flp-parse-cases(parse-json("local-plan",head),goal,band,flp-block(reply,"cases"),reference);
  }
  def flp-parse-cases(obj,goal,band,text,reference) = nothing?(text) ? (nothing?(band) ? ["band-unreadable","The reply needs <cases>...</cases> or an executable <band>...</band>.",[]] : flp-parsed(obj,goal,band,reference)) : !faj-valid(text) ? ["cases-unreadable","The cases block needs a JSON array. Use JSON null for Form's nothing() in arguments and equals; Form generates the native expressions.",[]] : flp-cases-parsed(obj,goal,parse-json("plan-cases",text),reference);
  def flp-case-value?(value) = fcgp-object?(value) ? false : fcgp-array?(value) ? all?(flp-case-value?,json-array-elements(value)) : true;
  def flp-case?(item) = fcgp-object?(item) && json-object-has?(item,"equals") && flp-case-value?(json-object-get(item,"equals")) && (len(json-object-pairs(item))==2 && fcgp-str-node?(json-object-get(item,"call")) && len(trim(fcgp-str(item,"call")))>0 || len(json-object-pairs(item))==3 && fcgp-str-node?(json-object-get(item,"function")) && len(trim(fcgp-str(item,"function")))>0 && fcgp-array?(json-object-get(item,"arguments")));
  def flp-case-value(value) = fcgp-array?(value) ? "[" + flp-join(map(flp-case-value,json-array-elements(value)),",") + "]" : json-emit(value)=="null" ? "nothing()" : json-emit(value);
  def flp-case-argument(value) = fcgp-object?(value) ? "parse-json(\"case-argument\"," + flp-said(json-emit(value)) + ")" : fcgp-array?(value) ? "[" + flp-join(map(flp-case-argument,json-array-elements(value)),",") + "]" : flp-case-value(value);
  def flp-case-call(item) = json-object-has?(item,"call") ? fcgp-str(item,"call") : fcgp-str(item,"function") + "(" + flp-join(map(flp-case-argument,json-array-elements(json-object-get(item,"arguments"))),",") + ")";
  def flp-source-path(path) = flp-starts?(path,"form-stdlib/") ? "form/" + path : path;
  def flp-case-check(definition) = json-node-object([fhn-s("tool","rg"),json-node-pair("arguments",flp-json-strings(["-c","-F",flp-file-bml?(definition[2]) ? "def " + definition[0] + "(" : flp-fk-mark(definition[0]),definition[2]])),fhn-s("stdout","1\n")]);
  def flp-case-plan(obj) {
   let writable=flp-strs(obj,"writable");
   let sources=flp-strs(obj,"sources") |> map(flp-source-path) |> filter(path=>!flp-has?(writable,path));
   let checks=flp-defs-of(obj,writable) |> map(flp-case-check);
   oh-set(oh-set(oh-set(oh-set(obj,"full",json-node-int(1)),"band",json-node-string(flp-tests() + flp-text(obj,"id") + "-band.bml")),"sources",flp-json-strings(sources)),"checks",json-node-array(checks));
  }
  def flp-cases-parsed(obj,goal,cases,reference) = !fcgp-object?(obj) || !fcgp-array?(cases) || nil?(json-array-elements(cases)) || !all?(flp-case?,json-array-elements(cases)) ? ["cases-shape","Each case needs function, arguments and equals, or call and equals. Expected values are scalars or nested arrays; observe object properties through the function.",[]] : flp-cases-balanced(obj,goal,cases,reference);
  def flp-cases-balanced(obj,goal,cases,reference) {
   let items=json-array-elements(cases);
   let bad=flp-first(0 .. len(items),i=>len(flp-delims(flp-case-call(items[i]),true))>0);
   nothing?(bad) ? flp-cases-owned(flp-case-plan(obj),goal,cases,reference) : ["case-delimiters","Case " + (bad+1).str() + ": " + flp-delims(flp-case-call(items[bad]),true) + "\nThe exact BML call: " + flp-case-call(items[bad]) + "\nUse function and arguments to let Form generate this expression, or complete the call before its witness is generated.",[]];
  }
  def flp-cases-owned(obj,goal,cases,reference) = flp-parsed(obj,(goal ?? flp-text(obj,"goal")) + "\nDefinition manifest: " + flp-join(map(d=>d[0],flp-defs-of(obj,flp-strs(obj,"writable"))),", "),flp-cases-band(obj,json-array-elements(cases)),reference);
  def flp-case-lines(state,item) {
   let id=state[0].str(); let call=flp-case-call(item); let expected=flp-case-value(json-object-get(item,"equals"));
   [state[0]+1,state[1] + " let result" + id + "=try [(" + call + ")] catch [];\n let actual" + id + "=nil?(result" + id + ") ? nothing() : result" + id + "[0];\n let expected" + id + "=" + expected + ";\n let held" + id + "=len(result" + id + ")==1 && actual" + id + "==expected" + id + ";\n print_str(json-emit(fcam-pack([" + flp-said(call) + ",value_kind(actual" + id + "),actual" + id + ",expected" + id + ",held" + id + ",len(result" + id + ")==1])));\n let all=all && held" + id + ";\n"];
  }
  def flp-cases-band(obj,cases) = "; Native case observations; the final reading is their conjunction.\n; Verdict 1\n; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-code-memory.bml " + flp-join(map(flp-token,append(flp-strs(obj,"writable"),flp-strs(obj,"sources")))," ") + "\nsection [form.bml] {\n let all=true;\n" + foldl(flp-case-lines,[0,""],cases)[1] + " all ? 1 : 0;\n}\n";
  def flp-parsed(obj, goal, band, reference) {
   let writable = if fcgp-object?(obj) then flp-strs(obj, "writable") else [];
   if (!fcgp-object?(obj)) then ["plan-unreadable", "The <plan> block is JSON but not an object.", []] else ["", "", flp-plan(fcgp-str(obj, "id"), fcgp-str(obj, "band"), fcgp-num(obj, "full"), writable, flp-strs(obj, "sources"), flp-defs-of(obj, writable), fcgp-node(obj, "checks"), trim(if nothing?(goal) then fcgp-str(obj, "goal") else goal), trim(band) + "\n", reference)];
  }
  // ── a verdict: [rung, kind, text, reading today, stub readings, reading with the reference, solofalls]; rung 0
  // holds; a solofall is [definition, full minus the band's reading with it alone at today's text (or nothing), the
  // checks that fail there] ──
  def flp-held() = [0, "", "", nothing(), [], nothing(), []];
  def flp-refused(rung, kind, text) = [rung, kind, text, nothing(), [], nothing(), []];
  def flp-held?(v) = (Comparable) v[0] == 0;
  def flp-with-readings(v, before, stubs) = [v[0], v[1], v[2], before, stubs, v[5], v[6]];
  def flp-reach(v, before, stubs, reached) = [v[0], v[1], v[2], before, stubs, reached, v[6]];
  def flp-falls(v, falls) = [v[0], v[1], v[2], v[3], v[4], v[5], falls];
  def flp-refused-after(v, rung, kind, text, falls) = [rung, kind, text, v[3], v[4], v[5], falls];
  def flp-falls-node(falls) = if nil?(falls) then json-node-null() else json-node-object(map(f => fcgp-maybe(f[0], f[1]), falls));
  def flp-checkfall-node(falls) = if nil?(falls) then json-node-null() else json-node-object(map(f => fhn-n(f[0], f[2]), falls));
  // ── (6) shape ──
  def flp-pow2?(n) = if (n < 1) then false else if ((Comparable) n == 1) then true else if (!((Comparable) (n % 2) == 0)) then false else flp-pow2?((n / 2));
  def flp-full-ok?(full) = if nothing?(full) then false else if (!((String) value_kind(full) == "int")) then false else flp-pow2?((full + 1));
  // the band sweep's reading: the first "Verdict N" on a ';' line before the first other non-blank line
  def flp-verdict-head(lines) = if nil?(lines) then nothing() else flp-verdict-line(lines);
  def flp-verdict-line(lines) {
   let l = lines[0];
   let at = str_find(l, "Verdict ", 0);
   let n = if (at < 0) then nothing() else flp-number-at(l, (at + 8));
   if flp-starts?(l, ";") then (if nothing?(n) then flp-verdict-head(lines[1:]) else n) else if ((Comparable) len(trim(l)) == 0) then flp-verdict-head(lines[1:]) else nothing();
  }
  def flp-space-free?(s, i) = if (i >= len(s)) then true else if (str_byte_at(s, i) <= 32) then false else flp-space-free?(s, (i + 1));
  def flp-path-safe?(p) = if ((Comparable) len(p) == 0) then false else ((!flp-starts?(p, "/")) && ((str_find(p, "..", 0) < 0) && ((str_find(p, "//", 0) < 0) && flp-space-free?(p, 0))));
  def flp-band-name(path) = substring(path, len(flp-tests()), len(path));
  def flp-band-path-ok?(path) = flp-path-safe?(path) && (flp-starts?(path, flp-tests()) && ((str_find(flp-band-name(path), "/", 0) < 0) && (flp-ends?(path, "-band.fk") || flp-ends?(path, "-band.bml"))));
  def flp-token(path) = if flp-starts?(path, "form/") then substring(path, 5, len(path)) else path;
  def flp-at(root, path) = if ((String) root == "") then path else mc-cat([root, "/", path]);
  def flp-bml-surface?(t) = flp-starts?(t, "section [") || (str_find(t, "\nsection [", 0) >= 0);
  def flp-fk-mark(name) = mc-cat(["(defn ", name, " "]);
  def flp-bml-mark(name) = mc-cat(["def ", name, "("]);
  // "def NAME(" at a line's first non-blank byte
  def flp-bml-find(text, name, from) {
   let at = str_find(text, flp-bml-mark(name), from);
   if (at < 0) then -1 else if ((Comparable) flp-indent-end(text, flp-line-start(text, at)) == at) then at else flp-bml-find(text, name, (at + 1));
  }
  def flp-def-in?(text, name) = if flp-bml-surface?(text) then (flp-bml-find(text, name, 0) >= 0) else (str_find(text, flp-fk-mark(name), 0) >= 0);
  def flp-def-present?(d) = flp-exists?(d[2]) && flp-def-in?(fhn-read(d[2]), d[0]);
  def flp-shape(plan, ctx) = flp-shape-at(plan,ctx,false);
  def flp-shape-at(plan, ctx, owned) {
   let id = flp-p-id(plan);
   let band = flp-p-band(plan);
   let full = flp-p-full(plan);
   let writable = flp-p-writable(plan);
   let defs = flp-p-defs(plan);
   let goal = flp-p-goal(plan);
   let head = flp-verdict-head(flp-lines(flp-p-text(plan)));
   let unnamed = flp-first(defs, d => (((Comparable) len(d[0]) == 0) || (str_find(goal, d[0], 0) < 0)));
   let elsewhere = flp-first(defs, d => (!flp-has?(writable, d[2])));
   let bare = flp-first(defs, d => (nothing?(d[1]) && (!flp-def-present?(d))));
   let unloaded = flp-first(writable, w => (str_find(flp-p-text(plan), flp-token(w), 0) < 0));
   if (!flp-kebab?(id)) then flp-refused(6, "plan-id", mc-cat(["The plan's id \"", id, "\" is not a kebab word: a-z, 0-9 and -, beginning with a letter, at most 64 bytes."]))
   else if (!flp-band-path-ok?(band)) then flp-refused(6, "band-path", mc-cat(["The band path \"", band, "\" is not a file directly in ", flp-tests(), " named <name>-band.fk or <name>-band.bml."]))
   else if (!owned && (flp-exists?(band) || flp-exists?(flp-at(flp-ctx-land(ctx), band)))) then flp-refused(6, "band-exists", mc-cat(["The band ", band, " already exists; a plan writes a new band and never rewrites one."]))
   else if (!flp-full-ok?(full)) then flp-refused(6, "full", mc-cat(["full is ", flp-show(full), "; it must be the sum of one power of two per claim: 1, 3, 7, 15, 31, 63 and so on."]))
   else if (nothing?(head) || (!((Comparable) head == full))) then flp-refused(6, "verdict-head", mc-cat(["The band's head declares Verdict ", flp-show(head), " where the plan's full is ", full.str(), "; the ';' lines at the top of the band must say '; Verdict ", full.str(), "' before its first other line."]))
   else if ((Comparable) len(goal) == 0) then flp-refused(6, "goal-empty", "The goal is empty: the <goal> block must say what the lane writes.")
   else if (nil?(writable) || (len(writable) > 3)) then flp-refused(6, "writable-count", mc-cat(["The plan names ", len(writable).str(), " writable files; a gap edits one file, at most three."]))
   else if nil?(defs) then flp-refused(6, "definitions-none", "The plan names no definitions: list each definition the goal adds or changes, with its params.")
   else if (!nothing?(unnamed)) then flp-refused(6, mc-cat(["goal-names:", unnamed[0]]), mc-cat(["The goal does not name the definition \"", unnamed[0], "\"; the goal must name each definition the plan lists."]))
   else if (!nothing?(elsewhere)) then flp-refused(6, mc-cat(["definition-file:", elsewhere[0]]), mc-cat(["The definition ", elsewhere[0], " belongs to ", elsewhere[2], ", which is not a writable file of the plan."]))
   else if (!nothing?(bare)) then flp-refused(6, mc-cat(["definition-params:", bare[0]]), mc-cat(["The definition ", bare[0], " is not in ", bare[2], " today, so the plan must give its params: {\"name\":\"", bare[0], "\",\"params\":[...]}."]))
   else if (!nothing?(unloaded)) then flp-refused(6, mc-cat(["band-loads:", unloaded]), mc-cat(["The band does not load the writable file ", unloaded, ": name ", flp-token(unloaded), " on its '; preludes:' line, so the band reads what the lane writes."]))
   else flp-held();
  }
  // ── (5) paths ──
  def flp-parent(p) {
   let at = flp-last-find(p, "/", 0, -1);
   if (at <= 0) then "" else substring(p, 0, at);
